I
1150 Version - synthetic test fixture, hand-written for tests/test_msa_db.cpp
*
* Layout copied from the real file; every value below is invented EXCEPT the
* shape of the records. Centre points are placed at whole degrees so the test
* can compute bearings by hand.
*
* TESTA -- centre at 45N 005E, four sectors, the classic four-quadrant chart.
*          Sectors run CLOCKWISE from their start bearing:
*            000-090 -> 5000 ft      090-180 -> 3000 ft
*            180-270 -> 4000 ft      270-360 -> 7000 ft
*          Note the 000 sector: a zero START bearing with a real altitude is NOT
*          the "000 000" terminator, and must survive parsing.
 1 TESTA TT TEST M 000 050 25 090 030 25 180 040 25 270 070 25 000 000  0
*
* TESTB -- same airport, a DIFFERENT centre point (an IAF), so records_for()
*          must return both and minimum_ft() must pick by centre ident.
 2 TESTB TT TEST M 010 090 30 190 060 30 000 000  0
*
* SOLO -- a single sector covering the whole circle, radius 10 NM only.
 1  SOLO TT TSOL M 000 025 10 000 000  0
*
* TRUEB -- bearings flagged TRUE rather than magnetic, so magvar must be ignored.
 1 TRUEB TT TTRU T 000 080 25 180 020 25 000 000  0
